Bound the leaf entry address in directory lookup (M2 task 13, fuzz finding).

Why: xfs_dir2_leaf_lookup_int() and xfs_dir2_leafn_lookup_for_entry() turn the
`address` of a leaf entry into a pointer into the data block and read
dep->namelen, dep->name and dep->inumber without checking that the entry lies
inside the block. The leaf block's CRC does not vouch for the address, so a
crafted image (address pointing at blocksize-4) makes the lookup read past the
end of the heap buffer. The kernel gets away with it because its buffers are
page backed; the backend's buffers are exact-size heap blocks.
Why not a shim: the pointer is formed inline in the two lookup loops.
Upstream: candidate (the same unchecked arithmetic exists in the kernel).
Behaviour: an out of range entry is skipped like a non-matching entry (the
buffer references stay balanced); the lookup then reports "not found".

--- a/xfs_dir2_leaf.c
+++ b/xfs_dir2_leaf.c
@@ -1344,6 +1344,16 @@
 			xfs_dir2_dataptr_to_off(args->geo,
 						be32_to_cpu(lep->address)));
 		/*
+		 * The leaf entry is untrusted (its CRC says nothing about
+		 * where it points): an entry that does not lie inside the data
+		 * block is skipped, never dereferenced.
+		 */
+		if (xfs_dir2_dataptr_to_off(args->geo, be32_to_cpu(lep->address)) +
+		    offsetof(struct xfs_dir2_data_entry, name) + 1 > args->geo->blksize ||
+		    xfs_dir2_dataptr_to_off(args->geo, be32_to_cpu(lep->address)) +
+		    xfs_dir2_data_entsize(mp, dep->namelen) > args->geo->blksize)
+			continue;
+		/*
 		 * Compare name and if it's an exact match, return the index
 		 * and buffer. If it's the first case-insensitive match, store
 		 * the index and buffer and continue looking for an exact match.
